From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:07:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(049): carry wasmtime 48.0.6 and rustls 0.23.46 for the
 reachable advisories

The packaged snapshot locks wasmtime and wasmtime-wasi 48.0.1 and rustls
0.23.45, and osv-scanner 2.7.0 reports 26 RustSec advisories against those
three crates on this PF's Cargo.lock. Upstream Zed main carries the same
versions at run time -- read 2026-10-17T16:02Z, main = 56934ec0560b
(committed 2026-10-17T09:29:58Z): wasmtime, wasmtime-wasi and
wasmtime-c-api-impl 48.0.1, rustls 0.23.45 -- so no Zed bump would bring
any of the fixes. This patch moves the three within their own release
lines and raises the workspace floors in Cargo.toml, so that a later
`cargo update` cannot step back below the fixed versions:

  wasmtime      = "48"      -> "48.0.6"
  wasmtime-wasi = "48"      -> "48.0.6"
  rustls        = "0.23.26" -> "0.23.46"

Operator decisions:

  * floors raised, not only the lock: 2026-10-11 for wasmtime and
    wasmtime-wasi, 2026-10-17 for rustls;
  * Config::wasm_exceptions(false) declined (2026-10-11): exceptions stay
    on. The fix is the version, not a feature switched off -- which would
    also have covered only the extension-host engine, not the grammar
    engine below;
  * rustls included in this patch (2026-10-17);
  * the seven-day release-age floor waived for this run (2026-10-17). The
    wasmtime, cranelift and pulley crates (48.0.6, 0.135.6) were published
    2026-10-14T16:57Z-16:59Z and rustls 0.23.46 2026-10-14T09:54Z, so they
    were 2.9 to 3.2 days old when adopted; the wasm-tools crates (0.254.2)
    were 15 days old.

Reachability, re-traced 2026-10-17 on this PF's tree (the trace with file
and line evidence is story 049's reachability record). Threat model for
every wasmtime row: the guest is an installed extension, hostile or
compromised. Zeo ships for Linux amd64 only. Two wasmtime engines run
extension-supplied code: the extension host (crates/extension_host,
wasm_host.rs fn wasm_engine: component model, epoch interruption, no fuel)
loads the extension's component, and the tree-sitter grammar engine
(crates/language, language.rs WASM_ENGINE: Config::new()) loads its
grammars/*.wasm modules. Compiled wasmtime features: gc, but only the
gc-null collector (asked for by tree-sitter through wasmtime-c-api-impl),
so GC types and exceptions are on in both engines; component-model-async
is off, so the component::concurrent module is not compiled.
wasmtime-wasi: p2 only (no p0, p1 or p3). rustls: aws-lc-rs with
prefer-post-quantum, no brotli, no ECH caller anywhere.

Reachable (6):

  RUSTSEC-2026-0314 wasmtime-wasi -- reachable: p2 is linked and the
    extension work dir is preopened read-write; a guest set-times with an
    overflowing timestamp panics the host in Duration::new (DoS).
  RUSTSEC-2026-0325 wasmtime -- reachable, extension-host engine: a guest
    component whose core module imports a mis-typed tag corrupts the GC
    heap (exceptions on); the advisory's impact is a host panic.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0359 wasmtime -- reachable, both engines: GC types are on
    and a guest-chosen long chain of recursive types overflows the host
    stack when the module is dropped (extension unload or reload).
  RUSTSEC-2026-0363 wasmtime -- reachable, extension-host engine: a
    component can resource.new without bound; Zed sets no ResourceLimiter
    and 48.0.1 has no store-wide handle cap (memory exhaustion).
  RUSTSEC-2026-0364 wasmtime -- reachable, both engines: a guest module
    with an odd number of exception tags mis-aligns VMContext fields
    (Rust UB; the advisory knows no exploit).
  RUSTSEC-2026-0349 rustls -- reachable, every HTTPS connection: with the
    aws-lc-rs provider, prefer-post-quantum and the default resumption
    store, an unauthenticated ServerHello pins a later connection to the
    same server name to classical key exchange (on-path attacker).

Not reachable (20) -- closed all the same, since the move fixes them too:

  RUSTSEC-2026-0315 wasmtime -- needs fuel; neither engine enables
    consume_fuel (the extension host uses epoch interruption).
  RUSTSEC-2026-0316 wasmtime -- only the dynamic component::Val API; Zed
    binds every API version with bindgen! and never builds a Val.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0326 wasmtime -- a stale GC ref needs a collection that
    frees or moves objects; only gc-null is compiled, which never collects.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0327 wasmtime -- needs component-model-async (not compiled);
    such components are refused at validation.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0353 wasmtime -- dynamic Func::call of an async-lifted
    export; Zed uses bindgen only, and async-lifted exports cannot validate.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0354 wasmtime -- the cancel-on-drop path lives in the
    concurrent module, not compiled; call_async runs on a fiber here.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0355 wasmtime -- streams need component-model-async; Zed
    creates no StreamReader.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0356 wasmtime -- stream/future results need
    component-model-async.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0357 wasmtime -- WASIp3 and Direct{Source,Destination}
    only; p3 is not compiled and Zed uses neither.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0358 wasmtime -- async-lowered imports and thread.yield need
    the async and threading component features, refused here.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0361 wasmtime -- the pending-call loop is the concurrent
    runtime, not compiled.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0362 wasmtime -- needs a host function re-entering wasm
    through sync APIs; Zed's host functions get no Store.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0321 wasmtime-wasi -- WASI p0 poll_oneoff; p0 and p1 are
    not compiled, and no fuel is configured.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0322 wasmtime-wasi -- only unconfigured stdio; Zed calls
    inherit_stdio().
  RUSTSEC-2026-0323 wasmtime-wasi -- WASIp1 fd_readdir; p1 is not compiled.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0324 wasmtime-wasi -- WASIp3 timestamps; p3 is not compiled.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0352 wasmtime-wasi -- affects macOS and FreeBSD only
    (RustSec os = ["macos", "freebsd"]; Linux renameat does not follow a
    symlink with a trailing slash), and Zeo is Linux-only. The path is
    otherwise live, so it IS reachable in upstream Zed on macOS.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0346 rustls -- needs a custom ClientSessionStore that
    formats session values; none exists in the tree or its dependencies.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0347 rustls -- needs EchMode::Enable; nothing calls it.
  RUSTSEC-2026-0348 rustls -- needs the non-default brotli feature.

