No source file needed a change. Measured 2026-10-17 (rustc 1.98.1) on
the whole series with this change: osv-scanner finds 66 advisories before
and 40 after, the 26 above gone and none new; cargo test -p
extension_host 45/45 before and after; cargo clippy -p extension_host
--tests 0 warnings, 0 errors. With only the ungrouped patches and this
one applied -- every USE flag off -- cargo metadata --locked --offline
accepts the lock as it stands.

Ungrouped: a security fix for every build, whatever the USE flags, so it
applies after the last ungrouped patch (0061) and before every USE group.
Of the later patches that also edit Cargo.lock, 0002, 0035, 0052, 0057 and
0058 are regenerated on top of it -- hunk positions and index lines only,
their headers untouched -- and 0036 and 0039 apply unchanged: their hunks
sit above the two dropped crates, so only their index lines would differ.
